<?xml version='1.0' encoding='utf-8'?>
<!--
	Appearance of the raid boss book, opened by right clicking the book item.

	Everything the player sees is defined here - every single string, every color and every text
	alignment included, so no player facing text is left in the Java. The behavior (whether the book
	exists at all, how many kills a hunting level takes, what a new level rewards, how many points a
	kill is worth and how much damage a hunting level adds) lives server side, on
	config/mods/raidbook.properties.

	Which item opens the book isn't set anywhere here either : the book is bound to an item by the
	"handler" attribute of data/xml/items ("RaidBossBook"), so any amount of items can carry it.

	The book holds three pages.

	The main list opens on a head telling the very player where he stands on the server wide ladder,
	along with a link to it, then the level filter menu, then one row per raid boss :

		Место: 12             1 250 очк.     Рейтинг
		============================================
		Все    1-20   20-40   40-60   60-80
		Greyclaw Kutus  Ур.23           ур.3   Инфо
		[############........] 2/5

	A book opens empty : a raid boss only shows up on that list once its owner has laid a hand on it,
	and it stays there afterwards. A list of the 213 raid bosses of the server tells a player nothing ;
	the list of the ones he actually fought is his own hunting record.

	Right under the head sits a search box, which narrows that list down to the names holding what is
	typed in it. It runs over the very list the page is built out of - a handful of templates already
	sitting in memory, sorted once at startup - so it costs one walk of that list and nothing else :
	no database, no world lookup, no index to keep. The typed text rides along every link of the book
	afterwards, so coming back from a boss lands back on the narrowed list rather than on the whole
	one ; the "clear" link next to the box drops it.

	The head links to the ladders, and a ladder page holds a menu of its own : the daily ladder, ranked
	on the hunting points summed over every raid boss, the monthly one, ranked on the amount of days
	its players took the first place of the daily one, and the rewards of whichever one is shown.

	A row draws the name and the level of the boss on one line and the progress bar of the hunting
	level right under it - the way the experience bar of a character reads - followed by the kills
	done over the kills the next level takes.

	The bar is a table of its own, nested inside the cell of the row : its background is the track, and
	the image it holds is the filled part, stretched to the progress, so a full level covers the whole
	track. It has to be a table, since the client only handles the bgcolor attribute on tables - a
	bare cell can't be given a color of its own. Both that image and that table are drawn a pixel or
	two short of what holds them : something of the very width of its cell leaves the client no slack
	and gets wrapped onto the next line. A row of the main list is two stacked tables sharing one
	background color rather than one table, because a bar can't share a table with text sitting in
	columns of its own.

	On a detail page the bar and its counter are centered together, since that page shows one single
	boss ; on the main list the bar starts on the left edge, under the name of its boss.

	A detail page opens on the statistics of the boss, laid out the way the status window of a
	character is - two blocks of two columns, each opening on a caption band of its own, exactly like
	the shift click window - then the hunting block, the buttons, and the four tabs :

		      Боевые характеристики      the "statsTitle" band naming the section under it
		========================
		HP  ...   Exp ...          the pools on the left column, the rewards on the right one
		MP  ...   SP  ...
		Респаун 2-12 ч.  Убит 03.09 21:40   when it comes back, and when it last went down
		========================   the hairline cutting the blocks apart
		Физ.Атака  ...  Маг.Атака  ...
		Физ.Защита ...  Маг.Защита ...
		Скор.Атаки ...  Скор.Каста ...
		========================
		      Охота на рейдбосса         the "huntTitle" band
		========================
		Ур.охоты  3     Убийств    12
		Бонус урона 3%  До уровня   3
		      [############........] 2/5
		========================
		Назад          Искать     x
		Награды  Дроп  История  Рейтинг

	Every number of the statistics block is computed out of the template of the boss rather than out
	of a live instance : a boss which is dead, or simply not spawned yet, has to be readable too. The
	defences carry "RaidDefenceMultiplier" of config/npcs/bosses.properties, and the experience and
	the SP are what the very player reading the book would earn for a solo kill - server rates and
	level gap penalty folded in. The respawn window is read off the spawn of the boss - the fixed
	delay minus and plus its random spread - and written in hours.

	"Искать" drops a radar marker on the spawn point of the boss, which is what the arrow circling the
	character then points at. A boss standing in the world is marked where it actually stands. The
	"clear" link sitting right next to it takes that marker back off the map : a marker outlives the
	page it was dropped from, so dropping one has to be as reachable as undoing it.

	A ladder page is the same list, holding the position, the name, the clan and the score of each
	player, the row of the reader being written with the "self" color. Its menu links to the reward
	page of that very ladder, which tells what each rewarded position is handed - and when the next
	handout is due, read off the schedule of the task doing it rather than off a setting of its own.
	That page
	is laid out the way the shift click window lays out a drop list, since it holds the very same
	thing - items grouped under what hands them out : one group header per rewarded position, framed
	by the rules cutting a page into groups, and the items of that position under it, an icon on the
	left and the amount written right under the name. A position handing out several items simply owns
	several rows, and the header above them says once whose they are.

	The item icons come from data/xml/itemIcons.xml.

	<layout>
		Sizes of the generated tables. Every table of a page is generated out of the very same
		width, which is what keeps them aligned - never describe one on the HTM.

		width       : width, in pixels, of every generated table. Fed to the HTMs as %width%. Keep
		              it below 290, so the scrollbar doesn't eat the last column.
		rowHeight   : total height, in pixels, of a row of the main list, and of a row of the daily
		              reward page. Such a row is two stacked lines - the name and the progress bar,
		              or the item name and its amount - and this is both of them together : the name
		              line takes "groupHeight", the other one whatever is left. So keep it above
		              groupHeight, and roughly twice it.
		groupHeight : height, in pixels, of the one line rows : the filter menu, the tab menu, the
		              button row, the page selector, a group header, a column header and every row of
		              a detail page tab.
		headerHeight     : height, in pixels, of a single line of a two columns block - the
		                   statistics of a boss and the hunting block.
		headerLabelWidth : width, in pixels, of one caption cell of those blocks. A block is two
		                   columns wide, so the value of a column takes what is left of that column -
		                   ((width - headerGap) / 2) - headerLabelWidth - and the numbers are written
		                   with their thousand separators, so leave it room. A caption which doesn't
		                   fit wraps, and a wrapped line is taller than "headerHeight", which throws
		                   the bottom padding of the page off.
		headerGap        : width, in pixels, of the spacer sitting between the two columns. Without
		                   it the caption of the right column would touch the value of the left one,
		                   which is right aligned on the column edge. 0 drops it.
		lastKillWidth    : width, in pixels, of the caption cell of the last kill date, which is the
		                   one caption not cut out of "headerLabelWidth". That date is the longest
		                   value of the whole block - a day and an hour - and its caption one of the
		                   shortest, so the wide cell every other caption sits in would leave it too
		                   little room and the date would wrap onto a second line.
		titleHeight      : height, in pixels, of a caption band - the ones naming the statistics of a
		                   boss and the hunting block, and the one telling when the next ladder
		                   reward is due. Unused when every one of those labels is empty.
		searchRowHeight  : height, in pixels, of the search row of the main list. It holds a field and
		                   a button, both taller than a text line, so keep it above "searchHeight".
		searchHeight     : height, in pixels, of the search field itself and of the button next to it.
		searchInputWidth / searchButtonWidth : widths, in pixels, of those two. Whatever the layout
		                   width leaves of them is split between the running query and the link
		                   dropping it - that link owning a "pageWidth" wide cell of its own, so it
		                   doesn't read as the last letter of the query - so keep their sum well
		                   under the layout width, or the query is left no room to be read in.
		buttonBack / buttonFore : client textures the pressed and the idle states of a button are
		                   drawn with. The stock pair is the small one the datapack uses at a height
		                   of 15 ("sek.cbui94" / "sek.cbui92") ; the taller pair
		                   ("L2UI_ch3.Btn1_normalOn" / "L2UI_ch3.Btn1_normal") wants a "searchHeight"
		                   around 21, and the row height to follow.
		iconSize    : size, in pixels, the item icons are drawn at.
		pageWidth   : width, in pixels, of a single cell of the page selector - a page link or an
		              arrow - and of the "clear" link of a detail page. It is what keeps the selector
		              on a single line : the amount of shown links is whatever fits "width" out of
		              that. Raise it if a selector ever wraps.
		maxPages    : maximum amount of page links shown by the page selector, centered on the
		              current page. It only ever lowers the amount "pageWidth" already allows.
		nameChars   : amount of characters above which an item or character name is shortened, on the
		              last word boundary when possible. 0 never shortens - and lets a long name wrap,
		              which makes its row taller than the others. Those names own their column whole,
		              so this is roughly the column width divided by 6.
		bossNameChars : the same, for the name of a raid boss on the main list. It gets a limit of
		              its own, and a tighter one, because it shares its line with the level of that
		              boss ("Greyclaw Kutus Ур.23") - the level has to fit next to it, whatever the
		              name. Roughly (listNameWidth / 6) minus the length of "levelPrefix" and of the
		              level itself.
		ellipsis    : suffix appended to a shortened name.
		separator   : client texture of the hairline cutting a page into blocks and framing the group
		              and column headers. It is always drawn 1 pixel tall - the height a page is
		              padded up to counts on that. An empty value drops every rule.
		overhead    : height, in pixels, everything but the rows takes on the HTM - the hairline
		              above the page selector and the closing spacer. Substracted from pageHeight to
		              know how much the page has to be padded with. Only worth touching after
		              editing the HTMs. Rough guide : <br> 16, <br1> 8, a separator img 1, a
		              selector row 18. The stock HTMs add up to 27.
		pageHeight  : total height, in pixels, every page is padded up to, 0 - the stock value -
		              disabling the padding altogether, which is what keeps the page selector right
		              under the last row of a page whatever amount of rows it holds. Setting it back
		              to a height pins that selector to one single spot instead, whatever the page :
		              a short page is then padded up to it, which is worth a lot of empty space on a
		              book holding few bosses. Set slightly above the height of the dialog, it also
		              keeps the scrollbar shown everywhere.

		screenTime  : how long, in milliseconds, an informational message stays on the screen of the
		              player it is sent to. The chat always gets those messages ; whether the screen
		              gets them too is "RaidBookScreenMessages" of the properties.

		barWidth / barHeight : size, in pixels, of the progress bar of a hunting level. Keep barWidth
		                       a few pixels under the layout width, so the counter written next to it
		                       is left a column of its own.
		barCounterWidth      : width, in pixels, of that counter on a detail page, where the bar and
		                       the counter are centered together as one block. On the main list the
		                       counter takes whatever the bar leaves of the row instead, since the
		                       bar starts on the left edge there.
		barFilled            : client texture the filled part of the bar is drawn with, stretched to
		                       the progress ; the track under it is a background color ("barTrack")
		                       rather than a second texture, so a full level covers its whole track.

		                       That is on purpose : "L2UI.SquareWhite" and "L2UI.SquareGray" are the
		                       two hairline textures of the stock client and they read as the very
		                       same grey once they sit next to each other, so a bar built out of both
		                       showed one single block whatever the progress - broken looking while
		                       being right. A color can't be mistaken for the texture sitting on it.

		                       An empty value leaves the bare track, without moving anything.

		The five sets of column widths below must each sum up to the layout width, otherwise the
		rows of that table won't be aligned - a mismatch is warned about in the log.

		listNameWidth / listLevelWidth / listButtonWidth       : rows of the main list - the name and
		                                                         the bar, the hunting level and the
		                                                         counter of the bar, the link to the
		                                                         detail page.
		dropIconWidth / dropNameWidth / dropChanceWidth        : rows of the "drop" tab. The group
		                                                         headers are cut out of the same
		                                                         widths - caption on the left, group
		                                                         chance on the "dropChanceWidth".
		rewardIconWidth / rewardNameWidth / rewardLevelWidth   : rows of the "rewards" tab. The daily
		                                                         reward page reuses the icon one and
		                                                         gives its whole remainder to the
		                                                         name, since a reward row there
		                                                         carries no third column.
		historyNameWidth / historyClanWidth / historyTimeWidth : rows of the "history" tab.
		rankPosWidth / rankNameWidth / rankClanWidth
		    / rankPointsWidth                                  : rows of the ladders.

	<aligns>
		Where the text of a cell sits inside it : "left", "center" or "right", and nothing else - an
		unknown value is warned about in the log and falls back to the stock one. A column header
		always takes the alignment of the column it names, so those two never drift apart.

		listName / listLevel / listButton : columns of the main list. The "Инфо" link is right
		                                    aligned out of the box, so it sits as close to the
		                                    scrollbar as the layout width allows.
		barCounter        : the counter written right after a progress bar.
		statLabel / statValue : captions and values of the two columns blocks.
		dropIcon / dropName / dropChance : columns of the "drop" tab.
		group / groupChance : caption of a group header - a drop category, and a rewarded position of
		                      the daily reward page - and the chance written on its right.
		rewardIcon / rewardName / rewardLevel : columns of the "rewards" tab.
		historyName / historyClan / historyTime : columns of the "history" tab.
		rankPos / rankName / rankClan / rankPoints : columns of the ladders.
		menu              : every cell of a menu row - the level filters, the tabs, the buttons and
		                    the page selector.
		empty             : the label shown instead of an empty list.
		title             : the text of a caption band naming a section. A band owns the whole width
		                    whatever edge its text sits on ; "left" is what lines it up with the
		                    captions of the group headers.
		nextReward        : the band telling when the next ladder reward is due, which stands on its
		                    own rather than naming what opens under it.
		bar               : the progress bar inside its own cell, and the spacers centering it on a
		                    detail page.
		headerRank / headerPoints / headerLink : the position, the score and the links of the head of
		                                         a page.
		searchField / searchQuery : the search field of the main list, and the query being searched
		                            for, written next to it along with the link dropping it.

	<colors>
		Every color of the book, taken from the shift click window (data/xml/droplist.xml) so both
		read as one single feature. An empty value keeps the client default : a transparent
		background for a row, a plain white text for a label.

		row / altRow      : background of the odd / even bands of a page.
		name              : names of the raid bosses, of the items and of the ranked players.
		groupText         : caption of a group header, and of a column header.
		bossLevel         : level of a raid boss, written next to its name.
		huntLevel         : hunting level of the reader, and the level a reward belongs to.
		label / value     : captions and values of the two columns blocks.
		count             : amounts - the dropped ones, the reward ones and the ranking points.
		title             : the text of a caption band.
		barTrack          : background of the track of a progress bar, which the filled part is drawn
		                    over. An empty value leaves it see-through, and the length of the bar
		                    alone tells the progress.
		tab / activeTab   : tab links and buttons / the shown tab and the "Искать" button.
		filter / activeFilter : filter links / the shown level range.
		page / activePage : page links / the current page.
		self              : the row of the very player reading a ladder.
		disabled          : the label shown instead of an empty list.

		highChance / mediumChance / lowChance : chances of the "drop" tab, split by the two
		                                        thresholds below.
		highChanceFrom / mediumChanceFrom     : those thresholds, in percent.

	<labels>
		bookTitle             : title bar of the main list. A detail page titles itself with the name
		                        and the level of its boss.
		rankTitle / monthlyRankTitle : title bars of the two ladders - the daily one, ranked on the
		                        hunting points, and the monthly one, ranked on the amount of days its
		                        players topped the daily one.
		dailyTitle / monthlyTitle : title bars of the two reward pages which go with them.
		daily / monthly       : captions naming those two reward pages inside their own head.
		rankDaily / rankMonthly / rewards : the menu of a ladder page - the two ladders, and the
		                        rewards of whichever one is shown.
		nextReward            : caption put in front of the date the next handout of the shown reward
		                        is due. That date is read off the schedule of the very task which
		                        hands it out (data/xml/scripts.xml), so there is no second place to
		                        write it. Emptying this label drops the whole band.
		nextRewardPattern     : SimpleDateFormat pattern that date is rendered with.
		nextRewardUnknown     : shown instead of it, when that task isn't scheduled at all.
		searchName            : caption of the button firing a search of the main list. The "search"
		                        label below belongs to the radar button of a detail page instead.
		wins                  : appended to the amount of daily wins on the head of the monthly
		                        ladder, the way "points" is on the daily one. The leading space
		                        belongs to the attribute.
		statsTitle            : caption of the band opening the statistics of a raid boss, naming the
		                        two stat blocks sitting under it. It is the very caption the shift
		                        click window uses. Empty drops the band.
		huntTitle             : caption of the band opening the hunting block. Empty drops the band.
		daily                 : caption of the link leading from the ladder to the daily rewards.
		placeSuffix           : appended to a ranking position on that page, "1" reading as "1 место".
		                        The leading space belongs to the attribute.
		dropGroup             : caption of a drop group header, followed by the rank of the group -
		                        a boss reads "Category №1, Category №2". Every group of a raid boss
		                        carries it, since a raid boss isn't spoiled. Both this and the prefix
		                        below are what the shift click window writes.
		numberPrefix          : sits between that caption and the rank of the group.

		The captions below name the columns of the lists which need it - the ladders and the history.
		They are drawn once on top of their list rather than sliced along with its rows, so they stay
		readable whatever page is browsed ; they take the "groupText" color and the very rules which
		frame a group header, so both read alike. The reward and the drop tabs have none : a reward
		list reads itself, and a drop group header already says what sits under it. Neither does the
		daily reward page, whose group headers name the positions.

		colPos / colName / colClan   : columns of the ladders - position, character, clan.
		colPoints                    : score column of the daily ladder, which counts points.
		colKills                     : score column of a per boss ladder, which counts kills.
		colWins                      : score column of the monthly ladder, which counts the days a
		                               player took the first place of the daily one.
		colName / colClan / colTime  : columns of the history - killer, his clan, when it happened.
		levelPrefix           : put in front of the level of a raid boss, and of the level a reward
		                        belongs to.
		huntLevelPrefix       : put in front of the hunting level on a row of the main list. It sits
		                        in a "listLevelWidth" wide cell, so keep it short.
		details / search / clear / back / rank : the five links - the detail page of a boss, the radar
		                                 marker, the way to take that marker back off the map, the way
		                                 back to the list, the ladder. "clear" lives in a "pageWidth"
		                                 wide cell, so keep it to a character or two.
		rankPrefix            : put in front of the position of the reader on the head of a page.
		unranked              : shown instead of that position, to whoever holds no point at all.
		points                : appended to the amount of ranking points on the head of a page - a
		                        bare number wouldn't tell what it counts. The leading space belongs
		                        to the attribute.
		hunt / kills / bonus / nextLevel : captions of the hunting block - the hunting level, the
		                                   amount of kills, the damage bonus that level grants and
		                                   the amount of kills the next one still takes.
		maxLevel              : shown instead of the kills left, when "RaidBookMaxLevel" is set and
		                        the cap has been reached.
		tabRewards / tabDrop / tabHistory / tabRank : captions of the four tabs of a detail page.
		hp / mp / exp / sp    : captions of the first statistics block - the HP and the MP pools of
		                        the boss on the left column, the experience and the SP the kill is
		                        worth to the player reading the book on the right one.
		respawn               : caption of the respawn window of the boss, which sits on a line of its
		                        own under them.
		respawnRange          : sits between the two bounds of that window. A spawn holding no random
		                        spread at all is written as one single value instead.
		respawnSuffix         : appended to it, naming the unit it is written in - it is written in
		                        hours. The leading space belongs to the attribute.
		respawnUnknown        : shown instead of it, for a boss owning no spawn point at all.
		respawnPattern        : DecimalFormat pattern that window is rendered with.
		lastKill              : caption of the date the boss went down for the last time, which sits
		                        on the right of that window - a window means nothing without the
		                        moment it is counted from. It is read off the kill history, so it is
		                        the last kill of the server rather than the one of the reader, and it
		                        is written with "timePattern".
		lastKillNever         : shown instead of it, for a boss nobody ever killed.
		pAtk / pDef / atkSpd  : captions of the left column of the second block.
		mAtk / mDef / castSpd : captions of its right column.
		noClan                : shown instead of the clan of a killer who had none.
		empty                 : shown instead of an empty list - which is what a fresh book is, until
		                        its owner lays a hand on his first raid boss.
		notFound              : sent to whoever asks for a raid boss which doesn't exist any more.
		noLocation            : sent to whoever asks to be pointed at a boss which owns no spawn
		                        point at all.
		searchDone            : sent along the radar marker.
		clearDone             : sent when that marker has been taken back off the map.
		titleSeparator        : sits between the name and the level of a raid boss on the title bar of
		                        its detail page. The spaces around it belong to the attribute.
		progressRange         : sits between the two numbers of the counter written after a progress
		                        bar - the kills done over the kills the next level takes.

		The four messages below are what the book tells a player about his own hunting. They all go
		to the chat ; the last three also go to the screen when "RaidBookScreenMessages" allows it -
		the kill one doesn't, it would flash on every single kill. Emptying one silences it.

		msgKill               : sent on a raid boss kill, to everyone credited for it. Holds the
		                        %boss% and %points% variables.
		msgLevelUp            : sent when a hunting level is reached. Holds %boss% and %level%.
		msgReward             : sent along each item a hunting level rewards. Holds %level%, %item%
		                        and %count%.
		msgDaily / msgMonthly : sent along each item a daily or a monthly ladder reward gives - on the
		                        spot when the winner is online, on his next login otherwise. Both hold
		                        %place%, %item% and %count%.
		msgBookGiven          : sent along the book itself, the first time its owner lays a hand on
		                        a raid boss. Holds no variable.
		countPrefix           : put in front of an amount, which tells it apart from the item name
		                        sitting next to it.
		countRange            : sits between the two bounds of a dropped amount which isn't fixed.
		chancePattern         : DecimalFormat pattern a chance is rendered with, its amount of
		                        decimals included. It is used by the damage bonus too.
		chanceSuffix          : appended to a rendered chance, and to the damage bonus for the very
		                        same reason - both are percentages.
		nearZero              : shown instead of a chance the pattern would round down to a bare
		                        zero, which would read as "never". Holds its own suffix, and is
		                        worth rewriting along with "chancePattern".
		timePattern           : SimpleDateFormat pattern a kill date of the history is written with.
		prevPage / nextPage   : labels of the page selector arrows. Both live in a "pageWidth" wide
		                        cell, so keep them short.

		A label needing a "&lt;" or a "&gt;" writes it as an XML entity, the way "nearZero" and the
		page arrows do. The book escapes them back on its way to the client, so a bare angle bracket
		would be swallowed as the start of a tag and take the rest of its cell with it.

	<filters>
		The level filter menu sitting on the head of the main list, one cell per entry, in the very
		order they are written here. They are cut out of the layout width, so adding entries makes
		every cell narrower - keep the labels short.

		label     : what the cell reads.
		min / max : the level range, both bounds included. A range of 0 to 0 matches every raid boss,
		            which is what the "Все" entry is.
-->
<list>
